-- California Bus. & Prof. Code Chapter 25.1 (TFAIA, SB 53) -- INDEPENDENT TESTS.
-- A DRAFT. Not for use as advice.
--
-- Written by a session that did not see the encoding being built. Every expected
-- value was decided from the deposited sources (the chapter, the chaptered bill and
-- Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12, 12a in registers/source-bundle/) and written down in
-- tests-independent-answers-first.md BEFORE the encoding was opened; the encoding
-- was then read only to learn its names and types. No expectation was adjusted to
-- match the code. A failing assertion here is a finding, left failing on purpose;
-- each one carries a comment naming the provision and the reading behind it.
-- Weekdays come from the system calendar. Holidays: as first written, the deposited text
-- named only Saturday (Code Civ. Proc. § 12a(a)), so each date edge was asserted twice:
-- with no listed holiday and with the § 135 days a reader would list (then recalled, not
-- checked: Sundays, 1 January, Thanksgiving, and the day after Thanksgiving).
-- REVISED 2026-10-24 after Code Civ. Proc. §§ 12b, 135 and Gov. Code § 6700 were deposited
-- (ca-time-computation-holidays-2026-10.txt, "holidays:N" below) and the encoding began to
-- compute Sundays: those four kinds of day are now read in the text (holidays:16, 21, 22),
-- and the nine assertions that assumed a Saturday-only rule were re-derived by hand; each
-- keeps its original as a comment. The "no listed holidays" assertions whose last day is
-- 1 January, Thanksgiving or the day after now test the encoding's input contract (those
-- days must be listed), not the law; see tests-independent-answers-first.md.

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay y m d MEANS Date d m y -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

§ `Independent fixtures`

-- Computing power, in operations (§ 22757.11(i)(1): "greater than 10^26").
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep: 10^25` MEANS 10000000000000000000000000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep: 10^26` MEANS 100000000000000000000000000
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep: 10^26 + 1` MEANS 100000000000000000000000001
GIVETH A NUMBER
`indep: 2 x 10^26` MEANS 200000000000000000000000000

