        (i's `the model's conduct`)
        (i's `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`)
        (i's `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`)
        (i's `the number of people who died or were seriously injured`)
        (i's `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property`)
        (i's `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model`)
        (i's `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`)
        (i's `there was a loss of control of the model`)
        (i's `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`)
        (i's `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring`)
        (i's `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`)
        (i's `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`)
        d hols declared inforce contract

-- The plain case: my own frontier model (2 x 10^26 operations), weights stolen and
-- someone hurt, no declaration, chapter in force, no federal contract.
GIVEN d IS A DATE, hols IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the Office of Emergency Services`
`indep: 15-day duty, plain case, discovered` d hols MEANS
    `indep: 15-day duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt` d hols FALSE TRUE FALSE

-- The expected "report" answer, built from my two hand-computed dates.
GIVEN fifteenth IS A DATE, last IS A DATE
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the Office of Emergency Services`
`indep: report to OES; day 15 and last day` fifteenth last MEANS `report it to the Office of Emergency Services` WITH
    `the 15th day after discovery` IS fifteenth
    `the last day, after any extension for holidays` IS last

-- The 24-hour question, foundation-model limbs all true.
GIVEN used IS A NUMBER, most IS A NUMBER, trained IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A `the incident as I know it`, d IS A DATE, imminent IS A BOOLEAN, declared IS A BOOLEAN, inforce IS A BOOLEAN, contract IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my duty to disclose within 24 hours`
`indep: 24-hour duty` used most trained i d imminent declared inforce contract MEANS
    `must I disclose this incident within 24 hours` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE trained used most
        (i's `there was unauthorized access to, modification of, or exfiltration of the model weights`)
        (i's `that access, modification, or exfiltration resulted in death or bodily injury`)
        (i's `the model's conduct`)
        (i's `the model materially contributed to the deaths, injuries, or damage`)
        (i's `the deaths, injuries, or damage arose from a single incident`)
        (i's `the number of people who died or were seriously injured`)
        (i's `the dollars of damage to, or loss of, property`)
        (i's `the harm came from information the model output that is otherwise publicly accessible in a substantially similar form from a source other than a foundation model`)
        (i's `the harm came from lawful activity of the federal government`)
        (i's `there was a loss of control of the model`)
        (i's `the loss of control caused death or bodily injury`)
        (i's `the model used deceptive techniques against me to subvert my controls or monitoring`)
        (i's `that happened in an evaluation designed to elicit that behavior`)
        (i's `that behavior demonstrates materially increased catastrophic risk`)
        d imminent declared inforce contract

-- The penalty question, foundation-model limbs all true, model trained by me.
GIVEN used IS A NUMBER, most IS A NUMBER, revenue IS A NUMBER, f IS A `a failure of mine`, n IS A NUMBER, inforce IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `what I can be made to pay for the failure`
`indep: penalty` used most revenue f n inforce MEANS
    `what is the most I can be made to pay for failing to report` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE used most revenue f n inforce

GIVEN per IS A NUMBER, total IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `what I can be made to pay for the failure`
`indep: AG-only civil penalty of at most` per total MEANS `a civil penalty that only the Attorney General may recover in a civil action` WITH
    `the most per violation` IS per
    `the most for the violations counted` IS total

GIVETH A `a failure of mine`
`indep: missed the 15-day report` MEANS `I failed to report a critical safety incident to the Office of Emergency Services within 15 days`
GIVETH A `a failure of mine`
`indep: missed the 24-hour disclosure` MEANS `I failed to disclose an imminent-risk incident within 24 hours`

-- Records for calling the reporting rule directly (the 15-day rule with the imminent-risk
-- fact set, which the baseline question always passes as false; and a large developer).
GIVEN revenue IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `me and my model`
`indep: my own frontier model, revenue` revenue MEANS `me and my model` WITH
    `the model is an artificial intelligence model` IS TRUE
    `the model was trained on a broad data set` IS TRUE
    `the model is designed for generality of output` IS TRUE
    `the model is adaptable to a wide range of distinctive tasks` IS TRUE
    `I have trained, or initiated the training of, the model` IS TRUE
    `the operations used to train the model so far` IS `indep: 2 x 10^26`
    `the most operations I have used or intend to use to train any foundation model I have trained or begun to train` IS `indep: 2 x 10^26`
    `the annual gross revenues of me and my affiliates in the preceding calendar year` IS revenue

GIVEN d IS A DATE, imminent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `my reporting position`
`indep: position` d imminent MEANS `my reporting position` WITH
    `the date I discovered the critical safety incident` IS d
    `I have discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury` IS imminent
    `my declaration under section 22757.13(i) is in effect` IS FALSE
    `the chapter is in force and not preempted as applied to me` IS TRUE
    `a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the reporting duty` IS FALSE

-- Holiday lists. Empty: the deposited text alone (Saturdays only). The others list the
-- § 135 days a reader would add (recalled, not checked).
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: no listed holidays` MEANS LIST
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: Sunday 2026-03-22` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 3 22)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: Sunday 2026-10-25` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 10 25)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: Thanksgiving 2026 only` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 11 26)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: Thanksgiving 2026, the day after, and Sunday` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2026 11 26), (YearMonthDay 2026 11 27), (YearMonthDay 2026 11 29)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: New Year 2027 and Sunday` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2027 1 3)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: Thanksgiving 2027, the day after, and Sunday` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2027 11 25), (YearMonthDay 2027 11 26), (YearMonthDay 2027 11 28)
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`indep: New Year 2028 and Sunday` MEANS LIST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1), (YearMonthDay 2028 1 2)

§ `(1) Frontier developer, large frontier developer`

-- § 22757.11(i)(1): "greater than 10^26". Exactly 10^26 is not enough; one more is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^26` `indep: 10^26`))
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^26 + 1` `indep: 10^26 + 1`
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26`
-- (h): "has used, or intends to use": a run begun with 10^25 used so far, intending 2 x 10^26.
#ASSERT `am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^25` `indep: 2 x 10^26`
-- (h) with intent at exactly 10^26: not enough.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^25` `indep: 10^26`))
-- (f): every foundation-model limb is needed (this model is the only one; none other over the line).
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0))
-- (h): someone else trained it; I trained nothing over the line.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0))
-- (j): "in excess of $500,000,000", developer plus affiliates, preceding calendar year.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000000))
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000001
-- Not a frontier developer, so not a large one, whatever the revenue.
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^25` `indep: 10^25` 1000000000000))
#ASSERT (NOT (`am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^26` `indep: 10^26` 1000000000000))
#ASSERT `am I a large frontier developer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 10^26 + 1` `indep: 10^26 + 1` 1000000000000

§ `(2) Critical safety incident`

-- (d)(1) needs death or bodily injury.
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt`
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: weights stolen, no one hurt`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: weights stolen, $2bn property lost, no one hurt`))
-- (d)(3) needs death or bodily injury.
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: loss of control, someone hurt`
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: loss of control, no one hurt`))
-- (d)(4): the only no-harm kind; not inside an eliciting evaluation; needs materially increased risk.
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: deception outside an evaluation, risk materially up`
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: deception inside an eliciting evaluation`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: deception, no materially increased risk`))
-- A near miss of any other kind is not a critical safety incident.
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: nothing happened (a near miss)`))
-- (d)(2) via (c)(1): more than 50 people.
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: CBRN` TRUE TRUE 51 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: CBRN` TRUE TRUE 50 0 FALSE FALSE)))
-- F4 reading A: harm short of the catastrophic size is not "materialization" (3 injured).
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: CBRN` TRUE TRUE 3 0 FALSE FALSE)))
-- (d)(2) via (c)(1): more than $1,000,000,000.
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: autonomous cyberattack` TRUE TRUE 0 1000000000 FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: autonomous cyberattack` TRUE TRUE 0 1000000001 FALSE FALSE)
-- (c)(1)(C) evasion of control counts; material contribution and a single incident are needed.
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: evaded control` TRUE TRUE 51 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: evaded control` FALSE TRUE 51 0 FALSE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: evaded control` TRUE FALSE 51 0 FALSE FALSE)))
-- (c)(2)(A), (B) exclusions.
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: CBRN` TRUE TRUE 51 0 TRUE FALSE)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: autonomous cyberattack` TRUE TRUE 51 0 FALSE TRUE)))
-- Harm at catastrophic size but none of (c)(1)(A)-(C).
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 2 x 10^26` (`indep: catastrophe` `indep: no (c)(1) conduct` TRUE TRUE 1000 0 FALSE FALSE)))
-- Every kind needs a frontier model: exactly 10^26 is not one; 10^26 + 1 is.
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 10^26` `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt`))
#ASSERT `indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 10^26 + 1` `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt`
#ASSERT (NOT (`indep: CSI with a model of` `indep: 10^25` `indep: deception outside an evaluation, risk materially up`))
-- A model that fails a foundation-model limb is no frontier model, however much compute.
#ASSERT (NOT (`is this a critical safety incident` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE `indep: no (c)(1) conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `is this a critical safety incident` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE TRUE `indep: no (c)(1) conduct` FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

