§ `(5), (6) Who the penalty reaches, and how much`

-- § 22757.15(a): a LARGE frontier developer; at most $1,000,000 per violation; (b) only the AG.
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 1 TRUE EQUALS `indep: AG-only civil penalty of at most` 1000000 1000000
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 3 TRUE EQUALS `indep: AG-only civil penalty of at most` 1000000 3000000
-- Exactly $500,000,000: not large, so no penalty under this chapter, though the duty was owed.
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000000 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 100000000 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
-- Not a frontier developer at all, however large its revenue.
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 10^25` `indep: 10^25` 1000000000000 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`
-- Chapter displaced (SEC. 5(e) input).
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep: missed the 15-day report` 1 FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I have said the chapter is not in force, or is preempted, as applied to me, for the penalty`
-- FAILS (finding; the text is open, see answers-first, "After reading the encoding").
-- F13 (my answers-first): a missed (c)(2) disclosure is "fail[ing] to report an incident as
-- required by Section 22757.13" (bpc:132), so the same penalty applies. The encoding answers
-- "only if section 22757.15 reaches" it (its F14). (c)(2) says "disclose ... to an authority",
-- (c)(1) "report ... to the Office", and (c)(3) speaks of "the initial report required by this
-- subdivision" (bpc:92-94): the verbs differ, so my "yes" is one reading, not the text.
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 500000001 `indep: missed the 24-hour disclosure` 1 TRUE EQUALS `indep: AG-only civil penalty of at most` 1000000 1000000
-- A non-large developer that missed the 24-hour disclosure: no penalty either way.
#ASSERT `indep: penalty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` 0 `indep: missed the 24-hour disclosure` 1 TRUE EQUALS `no civil penalty under section 22757.15, because I am not a large frontier developer`

§ `(7) Deemed compliance and the uncodified switch-offs`

-- § 22757.13(i)(2)(A): after a declaration in effect, deemed in compliance to the extent the
-- federal standard is met; (B) failing it is a violation. Both duties are in "this section".
#ASSERT `indep: 15-day duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) `indep: no listed holidays` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the chapter`
#ASSERT `indep: 24-hour duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: loss of control, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `deemed in compliance with the 24-hour disclosure to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the chapter`
-- Declaration off: the duty as written (the plain-case asserts above).
-- SEC. 5(e) (preemption) and SEC. 5(d) (strictly conflicting federal contract).
#ASSERT `indep: 15-day duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) `indep: no listed holidays` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I have said the chapter is not in force, or is preempted, as applied to me`
#ASSERT `indep: 15-day duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: weights stolen, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) `indep: no listed holidays` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered, because a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the reporting duty`
#ASSERT `indep: 24-hour duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: loss of control, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I have said the chapter is not in force, or is preempted, as applied to me, for the 24-hour disclosure`
#ASSERT `indep: 24-hour duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: loss of control, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 6) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not covered, because a contract between a federal government entity and me strictly conflicts with the 24-hour disclosure`
#ASSERT `indep: 24-hour duty` `indep: 2 x 10^26` `indep: 2 x 10^26` TRUE `indep: loss of control, someone hurt` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered, because I discovered the incident before the chapter took effect on 1 January 2026, for the 24-hour disclosure`

§ `(8) Confidentiality; (9) what the chapter does not contain`

-- § 22757.13(f): a CSI report submitted to OES is exempt from the Public Records Act.
#ASSERT `is my report exempt from public records requests` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`is my report exempt from public records requests` FALSE))
-- § 22757.13(a)(1)-(4): what OES's mechanism takes, and nothing else.
#ASSERT `what must my report give` EQUALS (LIST `item 1, the date of the critical safety incident`, `item 2, the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`, `item 3, a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`, `item 4, whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`)
-- § 22757.13(c)(3): an amended report is permitted ("may"), only after an initial report and new information.
#ASSERT `may I file an amended report` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`may I file an amended report` FALSE FALSE))
